Z||000000||polomeno||09-04-2001||06:05 PM||||Hey guys.. I was getting a annoying clicking sound from the top of the engine, i assume it was a sticky lifter, now I dont hear the clicking noise anymore .. BUT i am burning oil like crazy.. after i start car between 30 secs-1 min the engine starts to shoot out whitish blue smoke from exhaust.. is it possible lifter got stuck and valve is now stuck open and letting oil in? any suggestions?<P>thanks all<P>John||||reg||1
Z||000001||ray b||09-04-2001||06:16 PM||||valves can jam, but oil??<BR>a leak down test will tell<BR>pump comp/air in and listen to where it goes<BR>out at and look at pressure drop rate<BR>ck it out quick befor........<P>------------------<BR>Question wonder and be wierd<p>[This message has been edited by ray b (edited 09-04-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||watts||09-04-2001||06:17 PM||||Whitish tends more to mean a blown head gasket (water vapour).  Check your rad for signs of an oil slick, and check your dipstick for whitish/brownish mush on it.<P>Valves CAN stick open, but it's not too common.  And if it is, it'll run like CRAP since you'll have no compression on that cylinder!<P>Do a cylinder leakdown test I'd say for starters.<BR>||||reg||1
Z||000003||polomeno||09-04-2001||06:26 PM||||I just find it odd that the clicking would stop just as the engine starts to do that.. and if it was my head gasket, ( which is just got done 5 weeks ago for $600 for a blown gasket) would i not overheat? which i am not.. so far i'm not driving it..||||reg||1
